module nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection
module cellTrackingAnalysis
module doseResponseDetection

manifest NIH3T3_p65GFP_Cells
manifest PBS
manifest CompleteMedia
manifest PluronicF127
manifest TNFalpha_Stock
manifest LPS_Stock
manifest NuclearMarkerDye
manifest ImagingBuffer
manifest FC40_Oil

// ============================================================
// NF-kappaB Signaling, Dynamic Range and Stochastic Switching
// under TNF-alpha and LPS Stimulation
// Tay S, Lee TK, Hughey J, Leyrat A, Covert M, Quake SR
// Stanford University -- Bioengineering / HHMI
//
// Reference: Tay et al., "NF-kappaB signaling dynamic range in
// response to TNF and LPS" (in preparation at time of abstract)
// Platform: Gomez-Sjoberg et al. (2007) Anal. Chem. fully
// automated microfluidic cell culture system.
//
// EXPERIMENTAL OVERVIEW:
//   >3000 NIH-3T3 p65-GFP cells measured simultaneously
//   under 8 doses of TNF-alpha AND 8 doses of LPS (4 orders of
//   magnitude each), 6-min temporal resolution over 12 hours.
//   Nuclear p65-GFP localization tracked by fluorescent
//   time-lapse microscopy with custom nuclear-marker software.
//
// KEY FINDINGS ENCODED:
//   A. TNF-alpha oscillations at single-cell level are continuous
//      (not damped), confirmed by 12-hour extended time-lapse.
//   B. Dose-dependent threshold, dynamic range, and response
//      time (hundreds of min near threshold; <30 min at
//      saturating doses). NF-kappaB model (Kearns & Hoffman 2009)
//      modified to explain dose-response kinetics.
//   C. Single-cell variability: stereotyped at high dose,
//      stochastic switching near threshold from small
//      fluctuations in key protein levels.
//   D. Analog (TNF-alpha: graded, proportional) vs. Digital
//      (LPS: all-or-nothing, full nuclear localisation even
//      at lowest doses) signaling paradigm.
//
// NOTE ON DOSE ABSTRACTION:
//   The paper uses 8 doses per ligand spanning 4 orders of
//   magnitude. BioScript does not support numeric parametric
//   looping. Each dose arm is encoded as an independent
//   serial dilution from stock, using the same chained-
//   dispense pattern established in moazami_world_to_chip_dmf.bs
//   (b1/b2/b3 approach) to avoid compiler array-split issues.
//   Three representative doses are encoded per ligand:
//     Dose 1 = near-saturating (1:1 dilution from stock)
//     Dose 2 = intermediate    (1:10 dilution)
//     Dose 3 = near-threshold  (1:100 dilution)
//   These three tiers capture the full behavioral repertoire:
//   stereotyped oscillations, stochastic switching, and
//   sub-threshold silence.
//
// NOTE ON MICROFLUIDIC PLATFORM ABSTRACTION:
//   The Gomez-Sjoberg (2007) platform uses pressure-driven
//   flow through PDMS microchannels with on-chip valves,
//   not DMF electrode actuation. `mix` steps here abstract
//   channel-based reagent delivery and media exchange events.
//   `heat` steps model the on-chip incubator (37 C / 5% CO2).
//   The nuclear marker delivery and imaging readout are
//   abstracted through nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection and
//   cellTrackingAnalysis modules.
//
// NOTE ON TIMING:
//   12-hour time-lapse = 720 min (BioScript: m tokens only).
//   6-min imaging interval abstracted into detect duration.
//   Response-time window for near-saturating dose: 30 min.
//   Response-time window for near-threshold dose: 300 min.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- device priming, cell seeding,
//                             nuclear staining, TNF-alpha arm
//   BB2  tnfHighPass       -- tnfHighSignal > 0: oscillatory
//                             response confirmed; dispose
//   BB3  tnfHighFail       -- tnfHighSignal <= 0: no response;
//                             drain
//   BB4  tnfHighJoin       -- join: intermediate TNF-alpha dose
//   BB5  tnfMidPass        -- tnfMidSignal > 0: stochastic
//                             switching detected; dispose
//   BB6  tnfMidFail        -- tnfMidSignal <= 0: no switching;
//                             drain
//   BB7  tnfMidJoin        -- join: near-threshold TNF-alpha dose
//   BB8  tnfLowPass        -- tnfLowSignal > 0: subthreshold
//                             stochastic event; dispose
//   BB9  tnfLowFail        -- tnfLowSignal <= 0: silent; drain
//   BB10 tnfLowJoin        -- join: LPS arm begins
//   BB11 lpsHighPass       -- lpsHighSignal > 0: digital ON
//                             (full nuclear); dispose
//   BB12 lpsHighFail       -- lpsHighSignal <= 0: no response;
//                             drain
//   BB13 lpsHighJoin       -- join: intermediate LPS dose
//   BB14 lpsMidPass        -- lpsMidSignal > 0: digital ON;
//                             dispose
//   BB15 lpsMidFail        -- lpsMidSignal <= 0: no response;
//                             drain
//   BB16 lpsMidJoin        -- join: near-threshold LPS dose
//   BB17 lpsLowPass        -- lpsLowSignal > 0: digital ON
//                             even at low dose; dispose
//   BB18 lpsLowFail        -- lpsLowSignal <= 0: silent; drain
//   BB19 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Prime microfluidic device with 2% Pluronics F-127
//         in PBS to passivate PDMS channel walls and prevent
//         non-specific cell adhesion before cell loading.
//         The Gomez-Sjoberg platform uses pneumatic valve
//         control; priming fills all channels at low pressure.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
primingMix      = mix primingPBS with primingPluronic for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Seed NIH-3T3 cells stably expressing p65-GFP
//         (NF-kappaB nuclear localisation reporter) into the
//         microfluidic cell culture chambers in complete
//         growth media. Allow to adhere at 37 C for 2 h
//         (= 120 min) before stimulation.
//         Cell density: sufficient to resolve >3000 individual
//         cells across the array in a single experiment.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts pressure-driven cell delivery
//         through channel network, not DMF electrode mixing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nih3t3Cells     = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_p65GFP_Cells
seedingMedia    = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
seededChamber   = mix nih3t3Cells with seedingMedia for 5s

heat seededChamber at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Deliver nuclear marker dye into imaging buffer for
//         co-staining. The nuclear marker enables automated
//         cell segmentation and tracking by the custom image
//         analysis software (used to extract nuclear GFP
//         localisation intensity at each 6-min timepoint).
//         Stain for 30 min at 37 C before imaging begins.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nuclearDye      = dispense 1 units of NuclearMarkerDye
imagingBuf      = dispense 1 units of ImagingBuffer
stainingMix     = mix seededChamber with nuclearDye for 1m

stainedChamber  = mix stainingMix with imagingBuf for 5s
heat stainedChamber at 37c for 30m

// ============================================================
// TNF-alpha STIMULATION ARM
// Tumor necrosis factor-alpha: cell-cell communication signal.
// Response mode: ANALOG (graded nuclear localisation
// intensity proportional to dose; sustained oscillations).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4 (TNF-alpha Dose 1 -- near-saturating):
//         Dilute TNF-alpha stock 1:1 with PBS to represent the
//         high-dose condition (near-saturating; top of the
//         8-dose range spanning 4 orders of magnitude).
//         At this dose:
//           - All cells respond (response fraction ~1.0)
//           - Single-cell response is highly stereotyped
//           - Response time to first NF-kappaB peak: <30 min
//           - Continuous oscillations confirmed over 12 h
//         Stimulation delivered by on-chip media exchange
//         through the automated valve network (abstracted
//         as mix). Time-lapse: 12 h = 720 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfStock1       = dispense 1 units of TNFalpha_Stock
pbsDiluteTnf1   = dispense 1 units of PBS
tnfHighDose     = mix tnfStock1 with pbsDiluteTnf1 for 5s

tnfHighStim     = mix stainedChamber with tnfHighDose for 5s

// 12-hour time-lapse imaging at 37 C; 6-min interval
// abstracted as continuous incubation at imaging temperature.
heat tnfHighStim at 37c for 720m

// Nuclear localisation detection: nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection
// module abstracts the fluorescence microscopy readout of
// p65-GFP nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ratio at each 6-min frame.
// Detection window: 720 min total; cellTrackingAnalysis module
// abstracts the custom single-cell segmentation and tracking.
tnfHighSignal   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on tnfHighStim for 720m

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: TNF-alpha high-dose QC gate
// Pass (BB2): tnfHighSignal > 0 -> oscillatory NF-kappaB response
//             detected; stereotyped single-cell dynamics
//             confirmed; dispose chamber contents.
// Fail (BB3): tnfHighSignal <= 0 -> no response (below
//             detection or cell loss); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (tnfHighJoin).
// ============================================================

if (tnfHighSignal > 0) {
    dispose tnfHighStim
} else {
    drain tnfHighStim
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: tnfHighJoin
// Dispose high-dose TNF-alpha QC signal. Proceed to intermediate
// dose arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose tnfHighSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5 (TNF-alpha Dose 2 -- intermediate):
//         Dilute TNF-alpha stock 1:10 with PBS (chained dispense
//         pattern: 1 unit stock + 9 units PBS).
//         At this dose:
//           - Partial cell activation (response fraction
//             intermediate between threshold and saturation)
//           - Single-cell responses are heterogeneous:
//             some cells oscillate, others remain silent
//           - Stochastic switching behaviour emerges from
//             small fluctuations in key protein levels
//             (modelled by modified Kearns & Hoffman 2009
//             NF-kappaB ODE model with added stochastic noise)
//           - Response time: intermediate (tens to low
//             hundreds of minutes)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfStock2       = dispense 1 units of TNFalpha_Stock
p1              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p2              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p3              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p4              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p5              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p6              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p7              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p8              = dispense 1 units of PBS
p9              = dispense 1 units of PBS

// Accumulate 9 units of PBS by chaining (avoids array-split
// compiler issues; same pattern as moazami_world_to_chip_dmf.bs).
pbsMix2         = mix p1 with p2 for 5s
pbsMix3         = mix pbsMix2 with p3 for 5s
pbsMix4         = mix pbsMix3 with p4 for 5s
pbsMix5         = mix pbsMix4 with p5 for 5s
pbsMix6         = mix pbsMix5 with p6 for 5s
pbsMix7         = mix pbsMix6 with p7 for 5s
pbsMix8         = mix pbsMix7 with p8 for 5s
pbsMix9         = mix pbsMix8 with p9 for 5s

// 1:10 dilution: (1 unit stock) / 10 units total = 0.1x stock.
tnfMidDose      = mix tnfStock2 with pbsMix9 for 5s

// Fresh stained chamber for this dose arm.
stainingMix2    = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_p65GFP_Cells
media2          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
nuclearDye2     = dispense 1 units of NuclearMarkerDye
imagingBuf2     = dispense 1 units of ImagingBuffer
seeded2         = mix stainingMix2 with media2 for 5s
heat seeded2 at 37c for 120m
stained2        = mix seeded2 with nuclearDye2 for 1m
stainedChamber2 = mix stained2 with imagingBuf2 for 5s
heat stainedChamber2 at 37c for 30m

tnfMidStim      = mix stainedChamber2 with tnfMidDose for 5s
heat tnfMidStim at 37c for 720m

tnfMidSignal    = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on tnfMidStim for 720m

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: TNF-alpha intermediate-dose QC gate
// Pass (BB5): tnfMidSignal > 0 -> stochastic switching and
//             heterogeneous single-cell dynamics detected;
//             dispose chamber contents.
// Fail (BB6): tnfMidSignal <= 0 -> no switching events
//             observed; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (tnfMidJoin).
// ============================================================

if (tnfMidSignal > 0) {
    dispose tnfMidStim
} else {
    drain tnfMidStim
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: tnfMidJoin
// Dispose intermediate TNF-alpha QC signal. Proceed to near-
// threshold dose arm (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose tnfMidSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6 (TNF-alpha Dose 3 -- near-threshold):
//         Dilute TNF-alpha stock 1:100 with PBS to represent the
//         lowest responding dose (near-threshold of the
//         8-dose range; just above the activation threshold).
//         At this dose:
//           - Very few cells activate (response fraction low)
//           - Stochastic switching events are rare and
//             irregular: cells turn on/off unpredictably
//           - Response time: hundreds of minutes (cells that
//             do respond do so slowly)
//           - Mathematical modelling (modified NF-kappaB ODE with
//             stochastic fluctuations in IkappaBalpha or IKK levels)
//             recapitulates the observed switching statistics
//         NOTE: 1:100 dilution encoded as 1 unit stock +
//         chained 99 units PBS. To keep the file compact, the
//         1:100 is approximated here as a second serial 1:10
//         dilution of tnfMidDose (1:10 x 1:10 = 1:100). This
//         is pharmacologically equivalent.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfMidDoseSerial = dispense 1 units of TNFalpha_Stock
q1  = dispense 1 units of PBS
q2  = dispense 1 units of PBS
q3  = dispense 1 units of PBS
q4  = dispense 1 units of PBS
q5  = dispense 1 units of PBS
q6  = dispense 1 units of PBS
q7  = dispense 1 units of PBS
q8  = dispense 1 units of PBS
q9  = dispense 1 units of PBS

qbsMix2  = mix q1 with q2 for 5s
qbsMix3  = mix qbsMix2 with q3 for 5s
qbsMix4  = mix qbsMix3 with q4 for 5s
qbsMix5  = mix qbsMix4 with q5 for 5s
qbsMix6  = mix qbsMix5 with q6 for 5s
qbsMix7  = mix qbsMix6 with q7 for 5s
qbsMix8  = mix qbsMix7 with q8 for 5s
qbsMix9  = mix qbsMix8 with q9 for 5s

// First 1:10 dilution (intermediate level).
tnfSerial1      = mix tnfMidDoseSerial with qbsMix9 for 5s

// Second 1:10 dilution step for 1:100 total.
r1  = dispense 1 units of PBS
r2  = dispense 1 units of PBS
r3  = dispense 1 units of PBS
r4  = dispense 1 units of PBS
r5  = dispense 1 units of PBS
r6  = dispense 1 units of PBS
r7  = dispense 1 units of PBS
r8  = dispense 1 units of PBS
r9  = dispense 1 units of PBS

rbsMix2  = mix r1 with r2 for 5s
rbsMix3  = mix rbsMix2 with r3 for 5s
rbsMix4  = mix rbsMix3 with r4 for 5s
rbsMix5  = mix rbsMix4 with r5 for 5s
rbsMix6  = mix rbsMix5 with r6 for 5s
rbsMix7  = mix rbsMix6 with r7 for 5s
rbsMix8  = mix rbsMix7 with r8 for 5s
rbsMix9  = mix rbsMix8 with r9 for 5s

tnfLowDose      = mix tnfSerial1 with rbsMix9 for 5s

// Fresh stained chamber for near-threshold dose arm.
cells3          = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_p65GFP_Cells
media3          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
nuclearDye3     = dispense 1 units of NuclearMarkerDye
imagingBuf3     = dispense 1 units of ImagingBuffer
seeded3         = mix cells3 with media3 for 5s
heat seeded3 at 37c for 120m
stained3        = mix seeded3 with nuclearDye3 for 1m
stainedChamber3 = mix stained3 with imagingBuf3 for 5s
heat stainedChamber3 at 37c for 30m

tnfLowStim      = mix stainedChamber3 with tnfLowDose for 5s
heat tnfLowStim at 37c for 720m

tnfLowSignal    = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on tnfLowStim for 720m

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: TNF-alpha near-threshold QC gate
// Pass (BB8): tnfLowSignal > 0 -> rare stochastic switching
//             events detected above noise floor; dispose.
// Fail (BB9): tnfLowSignal <= 0 -> fully silent (below
//             activation threshold); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (tnfLowJoin).
// ============================================================

if (tnfLowSignal > 0) {
    dispose tnfLowStim
} else {
    drain tnfLowStim
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: tnfLowJoin
// Dispose near-threshold TNF-alpha QC signal. TNF-alpha arm complete.
// Control falls into LPS stimulation arm (BB11 onwards).
// ============================================================

dispose tnfLowSignal

// ============================================================
// LPS STIMULATION ARM
// Lipopolysaccharide: bacterial infection signal.
// Response mode: DIGITAL (all-or-nothing; full nuclear NF-kappaB
// localisation even at the LOWEST doses tested; cells that
// respond do so maximally regardless of LPS concentration).
// This contrasts with the graded analog TNF-alpha response and
// reflects the biological distinction between cell-cell
// communication (TNF) and pathogen detection (LPS).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7 (LPS Dose 1 -- near-saturating):
//         Dilute LPS stock 1:1 with PBS.
//         At this dose:
//           - Majority of cells activate digitally
//           - Each responding cell shows FULL nuclear
//             p65-GFP translocation (not graded)
//           - Response is indistinguishable from lower doses
//             in intensity; only response fraction changes
//           - Digital signaling: when a cell switches on,
//             all NF-kappaB protein localises to the nucleus
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lpsStock1       = dispense 1 units of LPS_Stock
pbsDiluteLps1   = dispense 1 units of PBS
lpsHighDose     = mix lpsStock1 with pbsDiluteLps1 for 5s

cells4          = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_p65GFP_Cells
nuclearDye4     = dispense 1 units of NuclearMarkerDye
imagingBuf4     = dispense 1 units of ImagingBuffer
media4          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
seeded4         = mix cells4 with media4 for 5s
heat seeded4 at 37c for 120m
stained4        = mix seeded4 with nuclearDye4 for 1m
stainedChamber4 = mix stained4 with imagingBuf4 for 5s
heat stainedChamber4 at 37c for 30m

lpsHighStim     = mix stainedChamber4 with lpsHighDose for 5s
heat lpsHighStim at 37c for 720m

lpsHighSignal   = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on lpsHighStim for 720m

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: LPS high-dose QC gate
// Pass (BB11): lpsHighSignal > 0 -> digital ON state
//              (full nuclear localisation) confirmed; dispose.
// Fail (BB12): lpsHighSignal <= 0 -> no digital activation;
//              drain.
// Both branches converge at BB13 (lpsHighJoin).
// ============================================================

if (lpsHighSignal > 0) {
    dispose lpsHighStim
} else {
    drain lpsHighStim
}

// ============================================================
// BB13: lpsHighJoin
// Dispose high-dose LPS QC signal. Proceed to intermediate
// LPS dose arm (BB14/BB15).
// ============================================================

dispose lpsHighSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8 (LPS Dose 2 -- intermediate):
//         Dilute LPS stock 1:10 with PBS (chained dispense;
//         same pattern as TNF-alpha intermediate dose above).
//         At this dose:
//           - Digital response still present; responding cells
//             show full nuclear localisation
//           - Fewer cells activate than at high dose, but
//             those that do activate maximally (digital)
//           - This distinguishes LPS from TNF-alpha: TNF-alpha at
//             1:10 would show graded, partial localisation;
//             LPS at 1:10 shows full localisation in a
//             smaller fraction of cells
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lpsStock2       = dispense 1 units of LPS_Stock
s1  = dispense 1 units of PBS
s2  = dispense 1 units of PBS
s3  = dispense 1 units of PBS
s4  = dispense 1 units of PBS
s5  = dispense 1 units of PBS
s6  = dispense 1 units of PBS
s7  = dispense 1 units of PBS
s8  = dispense 1 units of PBS
s9  = dispense 1 units of PBS

sbsMix2  = mix s1 with s2 for 5s
sbsMix3  = mix sbsMix2 with s3 for 5s
sbsMix4  = mix sbsMix3 with s4 for 5s
sbsMix5  = mix sbsMix4 with s5 for 5s
sbsMix6  = mix sbsMix5 with s6 for 5s
sbsMix7  = mix sbsMix6 with s7 for 5s
sbsMix8  = mix sbsMix7 with s8 for 5s
sbsMix9  = mix sbsMix8 with s9 for 5s

lpsMidDose      = mix lpsStock2 with sbsMix9 for 5s

cells5          = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_p65GFP_Cells
nuclearDye5     = dispense 1 units of NuclearMarkerDye
imagingBuf5     = dispense 1 units of ImagingBuffer
media5          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
seeded5         = mix cells5 with media5 for 5s
heat seeded5 at 37c for 120m
stained5        = mix seeded5 with nuclearDye5 for 1m
stainedChamber5 = mix stained5 with imagingBuf5 for 5s
heat stainedChamber5 at 37c for 30m

lpsMidStim      = mix stainedChamber5 with lpsMidDose for 5s
heat lpsMidStim at 37c for 720m

lpsMidSignal    = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on lpsMidStim for 720m

// ============================================================
// BB14 / BB15: LPS intermediate-dose QC gate
// Pass (BB14): lpsMidSignal > 0 -> digital ON state detected
//              in responding cell fraction; dispose.
// Fail (BB15): lpsMidSignal <= 0 -> no digital response
//              at intermediate dose; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB16 (lpsMidJoin).
// ============================================================

if (lpsMidSignal > 0) {
    dispose lpsMidStim
} else {
    drain lpsMidStim
}

// ============================================================
// BB16: lpsMidJoin
// Dispose intermediate LPS QC signal. Proceed to near-
// threshold LPS dose arm (BB17/BB18).
// This is the key result: even at near-threshold LPS doses,
// responding cells show full (digital) nuclear localisation,
// in contrast to graded analog TNF-alpha responses at the same
// relative dose level.
// ============================================================

dispose lpsMidSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9 (LPS Dose 3 -- near-threshold):
//         Dilute LPS stock 1:100 via two serial 1:10 steps
//         (same approach as TNF-alpha near-threshold arm).
//         At this dose:
//           - Response fraction is very low (few cells respond)
//           - BUT: cells that DO respond show COMPLETE nuclear
//             localisation -- the hallmark of digital signaling
//           - This is the key digital-vs-analog distinction:
//             at equivalent sub-threshold doses, TNF-alpha gives
//             weak graded responses while LPS gives full
//             all-or-nothing activation in a small fraction
//           - The modified NF-kappaB model explains this via the
//             TLR4/MyD88 upstream signaling architecture
//             producing a switch-like IKK activation profile
//             in response to LPS, unlike the graded TNFR1
//             response to TNF-alpha
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lpsStock3       = dispense 1 units of LPS_Stock
t1  = dispense 1 units of PBS
t2  = dispense 1 units of PBS
t3  = dispense 1 units of PBS
t4  = dispense 1 units of PBS
t5  = dispense 1 units of PBS
t6  = dispense 1 units of PBS
t7  = dispense 1 units of PBS
t8  = dispense 1 units of PBS
t9  = dispense 1 units of PBS

tbsMix2  = mix t1 with t2 for 5s
tbsMix3  = mix tbsMix2 with t3 for 5s
tbsMix4  = mix tbsMix3 with t4 for 5s
tbsMix5  = mix tbsMix4 with t5 for 5s
tbsMix6  = mix tbsMix5 with t6 for 5s
tbsMix7  = mix tbsMix6 with t7 for 5s
tbsMix8  = mix tbsMix7 with t8 for 5s
tbsMix9  = mix tbsMix8 with t9 for 5s

lpsSerial1      = mix lpsStock3 with tbsMix9 for 5s

// Second serial 1:10 step for 1:100 total.
u1  = dispense 1 units of PBS
u2  = dispense 1 units of PBS
u3  = dispense 1 units of PBS
u4  = dispense 1 units of PBS
u5  = dispense 1 units of PBS
u6  = dispense 1 units of PBS
u7  = dispense 1 units of PBS
u8  = dispense 1 units of PBS
u9  = dispense 1 units of PBS

ubsMix2  = mix u1 with u2 for 5s
ubsMix3  = mix ubsMix2 with u3 for 5s
ubsMix4  = mix ubsMix3 with u4 for 5s
ubsMix5  = mix ubsMix4 with u5 for 5s
ubsMix6  = mix ubsMix5 with u6 for 5s
ubsMix7  = mix ubsMix6 with u7 for 5s
ubsMix8  = mix ubsMix7 with u8 for 5s
ubsMix9  = mix ubsMix8 with u9 for 5s

lpsLowDose      = mix lpsSerial1 with ubsMix9 for 5s

cells6          = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_p65GFP_Cells
nuclearDye6     = dispense 1 units of NuclearMarkerDye
imagingBuf6     = dispense 1 units of ImagingBuffer
media6          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
seeded6         = mix cells6 with media6 for 5s
heat seeded6 at 37c for 120m
stained6        = mix seeded6 with nuclearDye6 for 1m
stainedChamber6 = mix stained6 with imagingBuf6 for 5s
heat stainedChamber6 at 37c for 30m

lpsLowStim      = mix stainedChamber6 with lpsLowDose for 5s
heat lpsLowStim at 37c for 720m

lpsLowSignal    = detect nfkbNuclearLocalizationDetection on lpsLowStim for 720m

// ============================================================
// BB17 / BB18: LPS near-threshold QC gate
// Pass (BB17): lpsLowSignal > 0 -> DIGITAL ON signal detected
//              even at near-threshold dose (full nuclear
//              localisation in responding cells); dispose.
//              This is the key result distinguishing LPS from
//              TNF-alpha: full all-or-nothing activation even at
//              the lowest doses in responding cells.
// Fail (BB18): lpsLowSignal <= 0 -> no cells activated at
//              this dose (below threshold even for LPS);
//              drain.
// Both branches converge at BB19 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (lpsLowSignal > 0) {
    dispose lpsLowStim
} else {
    drain lpsLowStim
}

// ============================================================
// BB19: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// Both stimulation arms complete. Experiment ends.
// Downstream: custom nuclear localisation intensity data
// extracted per cell per timepoint for:
//   - Oscillation period and damping analysis (TNF-alpha)
//   - Response time vs. dose curve fitting (both ligands)
//   - Cell-to-cell variability metrics (CV, noise analysis)
//   - Digital vs. analog signaling classification
//   - Stochastic model fitting (modified Kearns/Hoffman ODE)
// ============================================================

dispose lpsLowSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
